1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:03,870
Every midnight, the grid has to guess tomorrow.

2
00:00:04,800 --> 00:00:08,520
How much sun? How much wind? Hour by hour.

3
00:00:09,600 --> 00:00:11,670
This is Habagat.

4
00:00:12,600 --> 00:00:19,800
It replays six and a half years of NASA weather, hour by hour, at three sites across the Philippines.

5
00:00:20,500 --> 00:00:25,420
Pick any day, right up to June 2026, and watch it play out.

6
00:00:25,900 --> 00:00:32,290
Change the plant, and every hour reruns. Take the wind away, and the grid has to cover it.

7
00:00:32,740 --> 00:00:40,380
Then the forecasts face a year they've never seen. 2024. 2025. And 2026.

8
00:00:40,830 --> 00:00:44,530
Every day is forecast automatically, at midnight.

9
00:00:44,980 --> 00:00:49,420
Seventeen to twenty-nine percent less error than the best baseline.

10
00:00:49,970 --> 00:00:53,600
And grid plans that need up to a quarter less correction.

11
00:00:54,470 --> 00:00:57,160
Habagat. Read tomorrow's sky.

